# Observe Flame Blade's augment branch granting WQ_BURST to an already-flaming
# blade, for bd inc-wbq9 (PA-07-F9).
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/flame-blade-burst.keys 1
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED. The `flame blade;augment` effect's EV_MAGIC_STRIKE handler
# has two branches: a plain Short/Long Blade gets WQ_FLAMING, and a blade that
# ALREADY has WQ_FLAMING is promised Burst ("A weapon that already has the
# flaming quality is granted the Burst quality instead."). Before the fix the
# already-flaming branch re-granted WQ_FLAMING, so the blade gained nothing.
#
# THE ORACLE is the wielded weapon's own description: WQ_FLAMING reads
# "Flaming" and WQ_BURST reads "Burst" in the quality prose (src/Tables.cpp
# APreQualNames / APostQualNames, lines 1564 and 1568). The character starts
# with an orcish greatsword (WG_LBLADES), on the Right Shoulder.
#
#   i f SPACE   move the greatsword off the shoulder into the in-air slot
#   b SPACE     swap it into the Weapon Hand (the knife goes to in-air)
#   s           stow the displaced orcish knife
#   ESC         leave the inventory
#
# Wizard option 12, "Add Quality to Weapon", stamps WQ_FLAMING on whatever is
# in the Weapon Hand (src/Debug.cpp:722 InSlot(SL_WEAPON)) -- now the
# greatsword -- so the augment cast lands in the already-flaming branch. On a
# build WITHOUT the fix the sword's page still says only "Flaming" after the
# cast; WITH the fix it says "Burst" as well.
@include chargen.keys

# Put the orcish greatsword into the Weapon Hand.
i
f
SPACE
b
SPACE
s
@dump:wielded
ESC

# Wizard mode on.
w
y

# Stamp WQ_FLAMING on the wielded greatsword (wizard option 12).
@choose "Add Quality to Weapon"
"WQ_FLAMING"
ENTER

# Make Flame Blade castable regardless of class.
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Flame Blade"
ENTER

# Cast Flame Blade on self; answer "Augment or conjure? [aC]" with 'a', then
# choose the greatsword from the item prompt.
m
@choose "Flame Blade"
a
@dump:choose-item
a
@dump:after-cast

# Read the wielded weapon's own page: 'i' inventory, 'b' weapon hand, 'x'
# examine. Look for "Burst" in the quality prose.
i
b
x
@dump:weapon-page
ESC
ESC

@quit
